==Swedish==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|sv}} {{term|finna|lang=non}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|sv}} {{recons|finþaną|lang=gem-pro}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|sv}} {{recons|pent-||to go, pass; path, bridge|lang=ine-pro}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈfɪnˌa/|lang=sv}}
* {{audio|Sv-finna.ogg|audio}}

===Verb===
{{sv-verb-irr|finner|fann|funnit|finn}}

# to [[find]], to locate, to discover{{jump|find|s}}
#: ''Var kan man '''finna''' en kopp kaffe här i närheten?''
#:: Where can you find a cup of coffee near here?
# {{context|formal|lang=sv}} to have come to the conclusion, or opinion, that..
#: ''Jag '''finner''' det mycket märkligt att ingen kan ta på sig ansvaret för det inträffade!''
#:: ''I consider it quite remarkable that nobody can take responsibility for what has happened!''

